# Building this implementation

The converter is a standalone Go program. It uses only the Go standard library
and needs no downloaded modules, project-specific packages, or other converter
at runtime. A Go 1.20 or newer toolchain is sufficient.

```sh
./compile.sh             # creates ./executable
./executable --help

go test ./...            # regression tests, including a local HTTP server
```

The bundled usage documentation describes the supported operations. The code is
split into command-line/input handling (`main.go`), JSON-to-assignment formatting
(`forward.go`), and assignment lexing, reconstruction, and value extraction
(`reverse.go`). Regression tests cover observed formatting, sorting, sparse-array
merging, numeric spellings, Unicode, error handling, mode precedence, colors,
and HTTP/proxy behavior.

Generated executables and local experimentation files are excluded by
`.gitignore`.
